==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Magica Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Thaumaturge Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Weaken is vastly inferior to [[Slow|Slow]] and [[Freeze|Freeze]] in most cases but what makes Onmyoji Cat unique is her ability to target a wide variety of enemies, including [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] and, more importantly, [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies. Onmyoji Cat has a useful niche against threats that may otherwise prove impossible to consistently stall, such as [[R.Ost]], [[Bore]], [[Dober P.D]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]] and [[Primeval Cyclone]], but she is limited to weakening a single enemy at a time, making her ineffective against hordes and more adequate for "boss fight" kind of stages. She is best paired with units who can clear peons well, like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross]], as well as tanky meatshields who would really benefit from a less harmful "main source of incoming damage".

==='''True Form'''===
Thaumaturge Cat gains improved health and guaranteed weaken. There is thus no longer a risk of allowing the enemy to unleash their full power despite having this cat attacking it, nor is there a need to stack Thaumaturges, unless for safety reasons, since one cat alone is enough to perma-weaken. The difference between an enemy at full strength and a weakened one is incredible, so this True Form is worth unlocking even if it's not universally useful.

==='''Talents'''===
Thaumaturge Cat's [[Talents]] can be rather useful in certain stages. Immunity to [[Wave Attack|waves]] allows her use against the likes of [[Berserkory]] or [[Youcan]] to further reduce their pushing power while being able to pressure them. Resist Freeze prevents [[Henry]] from perma-freezing at any level, but there are hardly other situations where this comes into play. Resist Curse, while useful in presence of the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]], is no less situational as [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies can generally kill Thaumaturge outright. The stat buffs are not worth investing in, and if more health is needed for a particular stage catseyes should be used instead. All of the resists and immunities should only be acquired when you are struggling on a stage that it would be helpful for.

==='''Orb'''===
Thaumaturge does not need any orbs due to being a universal CC unit and having poor overall stats. However, if one possesses a Death Mini-Surge Orb, it can be used to great effect, due to her having a guaranteed Weaken.

